WEBVTT

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:10.820
So Ra No Wo To

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:47.940
Ready forward.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:48.900
Advance!

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:50.000
Advancing.

00:01:56.230 --> 00:01:57.740
Enemy sighted.

00:01:57.740 --> 00:01:59.010
Prepare to fire main cannon!

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:00.260
Distance 800.

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:02.600
Gunner, load HE round!

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:03.810
R-Roger!

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:06.850
Loading complete!

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:09.940
Prepare to fire!

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:17.780
<i>Fire!</i>

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:18.820
Boom!

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:22.440
Target hit!

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:24.300
All right. Signal the
forces to our rear.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.120
One enemy unit destroyed.
Follow me!

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:27.290
Roger!

00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:39.720
One enemy unit destroyed, huh?

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:42.000
Nice work!

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:43.770
We're not there yet.

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:45.810
Filicia, it's Claus!

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:50.600
My... Then let's have tea.

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:52.860
Good work, everyone.

00:02:55.380 --> 00:03:00.340
Mountain Hiking
- The Ends of the World

00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:07.380
Shuko's doing a lot better!

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:11.620
Her wound has healed,
but she's stayed here.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.400
Well, this place is wonderful, isn't it?

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:19.010
Hey!

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:23.140
How can she be that
active in this heat?

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:26.140
Yeah...

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:30.300
This is from HQ.

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:31.640
I need your signature here.

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:33.400
Here you go.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.900
And here are some letters
and packages for you.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:41.900
Kana-chan!

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:43.080
Yes?

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:44.780
Yes! Yes! Yes!

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.440
This is for you!

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:50.540
Thank you!

00:04:00.230 --> 00:04:01.850
It's from my mom!

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:03.690
And for you, too, Noël.

00:04:03.690 --> 00:04:05.050
From your beloved Professor.

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:07.140
Professor?

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:08.480
Yes.

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:12.640
His family name is Pro.
His given name is Fessor.

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:15.620
They're very common
names in Sept.

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:18.560
Mr. Fessor, huh?

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:21.880
It's wonderful that you have
friends from so far away!

00:04:23.140 --> 00:04:24.310
I'm sorry.

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:27.740
It was a joke.

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:37.390
Oh, come on, Noël.
I believed you for a minute.

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:42.970
Take Claus a present.

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:46.860
OK!

00:04:51.170 --> 00:04:52.430
Rio.

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:55.310
The usual.

00:04:57.210 --> 00:04:58.810
Throw it out.

00:05:00.010 --> 00:05:02.480
So, what did HQ say?

00:05:33.990 --> 00:05:34.990
Excuse me!

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:39.030
What's wrong, Kureha?

00:05:39.030 --> 00:05:41.730
Major Claus... Here!

00:05:43.930 --> 00:05:46.230
This year's, huh?

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:48.240
Yes!

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:53.960
U-Uh, th-thank you
for everything.

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:54.990
Don't worry about it.

00:05:54.990 --> 00:05:56.350
It's my job.

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:13.210
Major.

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:18.030
Here you are.

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:23.900
Roger.

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:25.260
I'll take care of the place
while you're gone.

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:25.990
Gone?

00:06:26.390 --> 00:06:28.860
Good luck out there, Private.

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:31.420
Thank you.

00:06:31.940 --> 00:06:34.850
Everyone, we're going on
a field trip tomorrow!

00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:36.200
Yay!

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:38.740
A field trip, she said!

00:06:38.740 --> 00:06:40.480
Isn't that great, Noël-chan?

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:41.670
Aren't you psyched?

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:44.060
A field trip... Filicia?

00:06:44.060 --> 00:06:49.720
Just walking would be boring,
so we're going to have a game, too.

00:06:50.230 --> 00:06:51.970
Game?

00:06:53.490 --> 00:06:56.020
You all know that there are
old-era observation devices

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:59.140
placed on the south side of Seize.

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:02.600
You know, the border between
us and no man's land.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:07.000
Three of them are up for their
regular maintenance check.

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:11.610
I'd like you to look at them
all on your trip.

00:07:12.350 --> 00:07:13.560
That's...

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:15.620
That's a mission!

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:18.290
No, it's just a field trip!

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:21.620
Even if they're broken,
we can't do anything about them.

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:25.980
Noctur-type observation devices
are a complete black box.

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:28.260
It's impossible to disassemble them.

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:29.800
So it's a field trip.

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:33.010
So this is what he meant by
"Good luck out there."

00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:35.990
But just walking isn't
good enough!

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:38.520
Thus...

00:07:40.700 --> 00:07:42.590
You'll be carrying those!

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:50.030
You're feeble.

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:54.530
Listen, the way to carry these is by
putting your weight forward...

00:08:00.430 --> 00:08:02.040
Wow!

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:07.540
I... I can't move.

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:09.550
Screw up.

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:11.800
Like you're one to talk!

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:16.850
You really are such good children.
You did exactly what we thought you would!

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:18.260
Argh...

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:22.100
Listen! When carrying
a heavy pack,

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:23.810
first, you lean back.

00:08:25.210 --> 00:08:26.310
Then...

00:08:28.130 --> 00:08:32.320
Once the weight of the pack
is completely on your back...

00:08:41.970 --> 00:08:44.340
Pathetic.

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:48.410
Stop talking...

00:08:48.410 --> 00:08:49.710
And do it!

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:50.800
Yes, ma'am!

00:08:54.930 --> 00:08:58.350
OK! Then Filicia and I

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:01.930
will proceed straight to the goal point
on the map to wait for you.

00:09:02.530 --> 00:09:05.940
If you really think you can't
go on, blow your trumpet.

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:08.440
We'll come to look for you.

00:09:08.570 --> 00:09:10.270
OK?

00:09:11.010 --> 00:09:13.760
And there are wild animals
on this mountain.

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:15.990
Should you encounter one,
I'll leave it up to you.

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:17.590
You have permission to use
your weapons if necessary.

00:09:18.140 --> 00:09:19.870
Got it?

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:22.620
OK, guys. Have fun!

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:26.230
Face right!

00:09:27.230 --> 00:09:29.400
Face right!

00:09:33.450 --> 00:09:35.130
Advance forward!

00:09:37.150 --> 00:09:38.850
Advance!

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:53.310
Now then...

00:09:55.590 --> 00:09:57.400
OK, the rest is up to you.

00:09:58.120 --> 00:09:59.410
Roger.

00:10:02.680 --> 00:10:05.410
Heavy...

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:11.330
Heavy! Heavy, heavy!

00:10:11.330 --> 00:10:13.580
Kureha-chan, don't say that.

00:10:13.580 --> 00:10:16.420
The more you say that,
the heavier it gets.

00:10:17.370 --> 00:10:20.620
Noël, how much farther?

00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:23.430
Noël!

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:36.160
Hey, Kanata!

00:10:44.860 --> 00:10:45.830
Found it!

00:10:47.300 --> 00:10:48.530
Yahoo!

00:10:56.620 --> 00:10:58.480
Wow!

00:11:10.280 --> 00:11:12.900
Functioning normally. No issues.

00:11:13.370 --> 00:11:14.420
What?

00:11:14.420 --> 00:11:16.520
We found that one easily.

00:11:16.520 --> 00:11:18.400
Let's keep it up!

00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:19.920
Yeah.

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:25.160
What's wrong?

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:27.510
No, just...

00:11:27.510 --> 00:11:32.660
I was just thinking, it's been protecting
the town, all alone, this whole time.

00:11:47.190 --> 00:11:49.720
Now then, Noël,
where's the next one?

00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:51.720
Let's see...

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:55.230
We're here now, so...

00:11:56.660 --> 00:11:57.790
That mountain.

00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:04.700
Th-Th-That mountain?

00:12:42.500 --> 00:12:45.980
Someone do something
about these bags!

00:12:45.980 --> 00:12:46.910
Heavy...

00:12:47.610 --> 00:12:52.890
I knew it. The captain and
Rio-sempai both hate me!

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:54.170
I know it.

00:12:54.170 --> 00:12:55.870
That's why they're doing this!

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:57.420
Heavy...

00:12:58.200 --> 00:13:02.630
Hey, say something, Kanata!

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:06.270
It's not like you not
to say anything!

00:13:07.960 --> 00:13:09.510
Hey!

00:13:09.800 --> 00:13:10.970
Shut up!

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:13.120
What?

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:14.280
I can hear you...

00:13:18.100 --> 00:13:19.270
I can hear you...

00:13:22.340 --> 00:13:24.090
I can hear you!

00:13:24.090 --> 00:13:26.530
Hey, Kanata!

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:29.000
What's wrong?

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:30.030
She's broken?

00:13:37.400 --> 00:13:40.040
Wow, amazing!

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:54.810
It's so cool down here!
And so pretty!

00:13:57.010 --> 00:13:58.440
Break time!

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:00.860
I don't care what anyone
says. It's break time!

00:14:01.470 --> 00:14:03.360
I've decided it!

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:06.610
First in!

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:08.240
Not fair!

00:14:15.870 --> 00:14:17.820
This is good!

00:14:20.600 --> 00:14:22.410
I'll get you for that!

00:14:23.660 --> 00:14:24.970
Take that!

00:14:31.940 --> 00:14:33.640
Just for the heck of it.

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:37.500
Noël, you...

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:43.900
A fish!

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:45.400
Hey, Kureha-chan!

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:48.010
Wow, this is fun!

00:14:48.010 --> 00:14:49.090
Yeah!

00:14:49.090 --> 00:14:52.030
No, it's not!

00:14:52.030 --> 00:14:54.240
You're not taking this
seriously enough.

00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:56.320
It's a field trip.

00:14:56.320 --> 00:14:57.650
You have to enjoy it!

00:14:57.650 --> 00:15:00.190
Did you forget about
those ten-ton sacks?

00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:02.450
This is training!

00:15:02.450 --> 00:15:04.340
But Filicia-san...

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:07.050
Get a clue already!

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:08.730
She's evil.

00:15:08.730 --> 00:15:10.170
The devil herself!

00:15:11.070 --> 00:15:14.020
But she's got blonde hair
and her skin is so pretty!

00:15:14.020 --> 00:15:17.220
That doesn't mean anything...

00:15:17.800 --> 00:15:19.350
Kureha doesn't understand.

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:20.540
Understand what?

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:22.500
That's what's good about her.

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:23.230
Right?

00:15:23.230 --> 00:15:24.650
No!

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:28.320
You guys must know
some other Filicia!

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:32.980
Geez! Someone do something
about these goody-two-shoes!

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:37.790
Time for food! Hooray for food!

00:15:38.130 --> 00:15:40.100
We're soaked...

00:15:40.100 --> 00:15:43.290
It'll dry quick in this sun.

00:15:47.540 --> 00:15:49.300
Wh-What?

00:15:51.480 --> 00:15:53.620
Our food's gone.

00:15:53.620 --> 00:15:55.920
Was it a boar maybe?

00:15:55.920 --> 00:15:56.860
What?!

00:15:56.860 --> 00:16:00.340
In the countryside back home,
they tear up fields all the time.

00:16:00.340 --> 00:16:04.560
But there's a lot of food for them in the summer,
so you normally don't see them.

00:16:05.190 --> 00:16:07.070
There's a bigger problem.

00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:08.380
What?

00:16:08.380 --> 00:16:09.710
The compass is gone.

00:16:09.710 --> 00:16:10.660
What?!

00:16:14.190 --> 00:16:17.830
I wonder if it was OK
to leave those bags.

00:16:17.830 --> 00:16:21.770
We've gotta focus on reaching
the goal now.

00:16:21.770 --> 00:16:23.330
Are we going the right direction?

00:16:23.990 --> 00:16:26.350
The first device was here.

00:16:26.350 --> 00:16:27.840
Here's the river.

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:32.640
We're on the mountain with the
second device at its summit.

00:16:32.640 --> 00:16:35.470
So we just need to head upward.

00:16:35.700 --> 00:16:39.480
OK! We'll get there,
no matter what-

00:16:43.400 --> 00:16:44.980
Hungry, huh?

00:16:45.290 --> 00:16:48.520
I wonder if there's anything
we can eat...

00:16:49.120 --> 00:16:50.210
There is!

00:16:52.750 --> 00:16:54.490
Bayberries!

00:16:55.380 --> 00:16:57.170
Can you eat them?

00:16:57.170 --> 00:16:57.830
Yup!

00:16:57.830 --> 00:17:00.490
They're sweet and a little
sour. They're good.

00:17:04.020 --> 00:17:05.210
The sounds made a chord!

00:17:05.690 --> 00:17:07.750
But we can't get up there.

00:17:07.750 --> 00:17:08.750
It's dangerous.

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:10.070
You think so?

00:17:10.070 --> 00:17:11.960
We should hurry.

00:17:12.270 --> 00:17:16.110
They say Major Claus once
crossed a desert in a tank,

00:17:16.110 --> 00:17:20.700
for three days and nights, with no food,
to take out an enemy fortress!

00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:22.220
We'll be fine!

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:23.360
Yeah?

00:17:23.360 --> 00:17:24.840
You've never heard that?

00:17:24.840 --> 00:17:26.820
They call him the Desert Wolf.

00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:28.230
He's amazing!

00:17:28.230 --> 00:17:31.890
Wow... Claus-san is?

00:17:31.890 --> 00:17:34.310
So let's do our best!

00:17:34.310 --> 00:17:36.170
But the bayberries...

00:17:36.170 --> 00:17:38.220
No whining!

00:17:46.900 --> 00:17:49.170
Found number two!

00:18:04.500 --> 00:18:06.380
A boar?

00:18:18.770 --> 00:18:21.080
Where's the last one?

00:18:22.190 --> 00:18:25.220
It's getting pretty dark.

00:18:25.220 --> 00:18:28.080
So we'll have to keep
checking our direction.

00:18:28.350 --> 00:18:31.140
Is this really the right way?

00:18:31.140 --> 00:18:31.960
Probably.

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:34.040
What do you mean, "Probably"?

00:18:34.040 --> 00:18:37.410
I can't be one hundred percent
sure without a compass.

00:18:37.410 --> 00:18:41.010
Then what? We've come
all this way for nothing?

00:18:41.310 --> 00:18:43.220
That's not what I'm saying.

00:18:43.220 --> 00:18:47.400
If the compass is that important,
you should've kept it with you!

00:18:47.400 --> 00:18:48.520
Hey!

00:18:48.870 --> 00:18:52.420
Let's not fight here, guys!

00:18:52.420 --> 00:18:55.450
It's your fault for playing
in the river.

00:18:55.450 --> 00:18:56.150
Huh?

00:18:56.150 --> 00:18:57.290
That's right!

00:18:57.290 --> 00:18:59.680
You're not taking this seriously!

00:18:59.680 --> 00:19:01.390
What did you mean, field trip?

00:19:01.390 --> 00:19:04.790
You're such an airhead,
smiling like an idiot all the time!

00:19:04.790 --> 00:19:07.040
That's why we're in this mess!

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:08.280
Don't you understand that?

00:19:08.280 --> 00:19:08.900
Hey!

00:19:13.050 --> 00:19:14.730
There it is!

00:19:19.840 --> 00:19:21.510
Yahoo!

00:19:22.350 --> 00:19:23.960
Hey, wait!

00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:25.660
Kanata!

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:30.780
Sheesh... I guess they'll be all right.

00:20:07.250 --> 00:20:08.520
<i>Goal!</i>

00:20:08.950 --> 00:20:10.320
We did it!

00:20:10.320 --> 00:20:12.250
We did it, Kureha-chan!

00:20:13.120 --> 00:20:18.800
I get it, I get it, so get off me!
I can't breathe...

00:20:19.300 --> 00:20:20.280
Look.

00:20:35.710 --> 00:20:37.040
<i>No Man's Land.</i>

00:20:44.140 --> 00:20:48.060
This is the end of the inhabited world.

00:20:50.230 --> 00:20:51.730
Good work!

00:20:53.710 --> 00:20:55.410
Captain, I'm sorry!

00:20:55.410 --> 00:20:58.490
We didn't complete our mission!

00:20:58.490 --> 00:21:00.400
What mission?

00:21:00.400 --> 00:21:02.240
Huh? But...

00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:04.690
I told you, it's a field trip.

00:21:04.690 --> 00:21:06.430
But...

00:21:06.430 --> 00:21:10.740
We just wanted you to see this.

00:21:11.690 --> 00:21:15.430
These are the signatures of
those who came before us.

00:21:15.430 --> 00:21:19.250
All the fortress maidens came
here at least once.

00:21:20.530 --> 00:21:25.260
And they saw this...
The end of the world.

00:21:30.690 --> 00:21:33.710
This is history, isn't it?

00:21:33.710 --> 00:21:37.810
It sure is... Can you
walk a bit more?

00:21:37.810 --> 00:21:41.820
There's one more thing
they've left us.

00:21:56.450 --> 00:21:57.920
You're late!

00:22:01.690 --> 00:22:03.630
Rio-sempai?

00:22:03.630 --> 00:22:04.800
What happened?

00:22:05.510 --> 00:22:07.130
Here!

00:22:08.550 --> 00:22:10.050
Bayberries!

00:22:17.460 --> 00:22:19.560
I feel alive again.

00:22:23.220 --> 00:22:24.890
So, did you win?

00:22:24.890 --> 00:22:25.880
Don't ask.

00:22:36.310 --> 00:22:41.280
But it was worth the effort...

00:24:14.930 --> 00:24:19.890
Kanata's Day Off - Hair Braiding

00:24:15.570 --> 00:24:16.850
Next time:

00:24:16.850 --> 00:24:18.260
Kanata's Day Off.

00:24:18.260 --> 00:24:19.370
Hair Braiding.

00:24:19.890 --> 00:24:24.900
This program is a work of fiction.
Any resemblance to people, parties,
or situations is purely coincidental.
